  "$comment": "Spec for the MapLibre sprite sheet. EDIT THIS, then run `py pipeline/sprite.py`. Patterns are tiled by fill-pattern and must be seamless - every primitive wraps at the tile edge. Icons are drawn in normalised 0-1 coordinates with y pointing down.",

  "$comment_look": "Hand-tinted historical estate map: saturated pigment laid unevenly, granulating into the paper, with crisp ink linework drawn over it. Each land class is a `wash` (uneven tint from tileable fractal noise) plus `granulation` (fine settling), then any structural marks - furrows, orchard ranks, hatching - laid on top the way an engraver would.",

  "pattern_size": 48,
  "icon_size": 24,
  "pixel_ratio": 2,
  "$comment_ratio": "Everything is rendered at this multiple and declared with pixelRatio, so it stays crisp on phones.",

  "paper": {
    "$comment": "Laid over the entire map by CSS multiply blend, so washes, ink and labels share one sheet. Larger than the patterns so the grain does not visibly repeat.",
